## Publication checks

Callisto checks the registry, remote tag, and GitHub release before each effect. An exact match is adopted; a conflict or uncertain result stops the run. Check the receipt and providers before treating a release as complete.
---

- Native npm lifecycle hooks can initiate effects outside Callisto's release-operation graph. Their behavior is package-owner-defined and is not inspected, rewritten, suppressed or rejected by Callisto; this is an explicit ownership boundary, not an automatic-enforcement defect.
- Registry version existence is not proof of identical package bytes or the desired npm dist-tag. A Python release is complete when every built file is on the index by name; sealing the file set in a build job and comparing digests of earlier uploads is the rest of T09. Universal checksum enforcement and channel promotion remain owner decisions.
- Cargo and PyPI real local registry tests exist in `release_real_registry_e2e_tests.rs`; they drive publisher argv directly, bypass production binding/observation in those paths, and can skip when tools are missing. npm has broader end-to-end coverage. Record exercised versus skipped paths; do not mark the missing Cargo test as the remaining v1 blocker (T12).
- Fresh local Cargo/npm/PyPI repositories completed documented setup through release dry-run; npm packing and Cargo package inventory passed. Python artifact build was blocked on sandbox network access to `setuptools`, and no timings, credentials, registry publication or hosted release were exercised. The under-ten-minute first-published-release goal therefore remains unverified (T12-DX).
---
    uploaded: Mutex<Vec<String>>,
}

fn io_error(error: std::io::Error) -> GraphError {
    GraphError::Command(CommandError::Io {
        program: "python -m build".to_string(),
        message: error.to_string(),
    })
}

/// Every wheel and sdist of `package_name` at `version` directly in `dir`, with its digest, by filename.
fn inventory(dir: &Path, package_name: &str, version: &Version) -> Result<Vec<BuiltFile>, GraphError> {
    let wanted = normalize_pypi_project_name(package_name);
    let mut files = Vec::new();
    for entry in std::fs::read_dir(dir).map_err(io_error)? {
        let path = entry.map_err(io_error)?.path();
        let Some(filename) = path.file_name().and_then(|name| name.to_str()).map(str::to_owned) else {
            continue;
        };
        let belongs = dist_filename_parts(&filename).is_some_and(|(name, candidate)| {
            normalize_pypi_project_name(name) == wanted && is_version(candidate, version)
        });
        if !belongs {
            continue;
        }
        let sha256 = format!("{:x}", Sha256::digest(std::fs::read(&path).map_err(io_error)?));
        files.push(BuiltFile { filename, path, sha256 });
    }
    files.sort_by(|left, right| left.filename.cmp(&right.filename));
    for (present, missing) in [
        (files.iter().any(|file| is_wheel(&file.filename)), "wheel"),
        (files.iter().any(|file| is_sdist(&file.filename)), "sdist"),
    ] {
        if !present {
            return Err(GraphError::PypiBuildOutputIncomplete {
                package: package_name.to_string(),
                version: version.clone(),
                missing,
            });
        }
    }
    Ok(files)
}

